 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization for\nimposition of additional sales and compensating use taxes in Greene county",
    "basePrintNo": "S6450",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6450-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6450\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization\nfor imposition of additional sales and compensating use taxes in Greene\ncounty\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill will extend the expiration of the authorization for Greene\nCounty to impose an additional one percent sales and compensating use\ntax to November 30, 2025.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 1210 of the tax law to extend the authori-\nzation for Greene County to impose an additional one percent sales and\ncompensating use tax above their statutory limit of three percent until\nNovember 30th, 2025.\n\nSection two states the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nThe current authorization to impose an additional sales and compensating\nuse tax in clause 15 of subparagraph (i) of the opening paragraph of\nsection 1210 of the tax law is set to expire on November 30th 2023.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Greene County Legislature passed Resolution 9-23 on January 18,\n2023, requesting that the New York State Legislature introduce and pass\na bill to authorize the County to continue to impose an additional one\npercent sales and compensating use tax for the period through November\n30, 2025.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect inunediately.\n",
